## The Arrangement of this Maha Buddhavamsa Text
If this great treasury of knowledge—the manuscripts which were the final hoisting of the banner of wisdom in Saya Gyi's life, being extremely extensive, full of noteworthy points, and profound in meaning—were printed according to the original arrangement, it would be difficult for the readers of the Buddha's life to read and remember, and it would be confusing. Therefore:
(1) Arranging the text of the Buddha's life separately;
(2) Revising and arranging the second chapter on the rarity of a Buddha's appearance (Buddhupādādullabha), and finalizing it only after obtaining the agreement of the Presiding Sayadaws (Nāyaka Sayadaws);
(3) Adding and writing the miscellaneous section (Pakiṇṇaka), which includes all the details that every person aspiring for Buddhahood must follow, know, and fulfill;
(4) Arranging the text of the Buddha's life separately and presenting the meanings, decisions, and noteworthy points in full as an appendix to Volume 1, Part 1, under the name "Anudīpanī";
(5) Changing some difficult terms and vocabulary into easily understandable Burmese vocabulary—
Thus, this Maha Buddhavamsa has been arranged and written.
When this Maha Buddhavamsa was printed at the Union of Burma Buddha Sasana Council Press, Saya Gyi Saya Nyan, the Chief Proofreader and Professor of Pali (Maha Panna Bala), supervised the proofreading.

